{"time": 1792012047.8676395, "direction": "server->client", "message": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"tools": [{"name": "ping", "description": "Send 4 ICMP echo requests to a host (network layer reachability).\n\nReturns packet loss percentage and average latency. Use it to check whether\na host is reachable at all, before testing ports or applications.\n\nArgs:\n    host: Hostname or IP address, e.g. \"8.8.8.8\" or \"www.ufrgs.br\".\n", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"host": {"title": "Host", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["host"], "title": "pingArguments", "type": "object"}, "outputSchema": {"properties": {"result": {"title": "Result", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["result"], "title": "pingOutput", "type": "object"}}, {"name": "dns_lookup", "description": "Resolve a hostname to IP addresses using the system DNS resolver.\n\nUse it to check whether name resolution works. A failure here means the\nproblem is DNS, not the network or the service.\n\nArgs:\n    name: Hostname to resolve, e.g. \"www.ufrgs.br\".\n", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"name": {"title": "Name", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["name"], "title": "dns_lookupArguments", "type": "object"}, "outputSchema": {"properties": {"result": {"title": "Result", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["result"], "title": "dns_lookupOutput", "type": "object"}}, {"name": "check_port", "description": "Try to open a TCP connection to host:port (transport layer).\n\nReturns state \"open\", \"closed\" (connection refused: host is up but nothing\nlistens on the port, i.e. the service is down), \"timeout\" (filtered or host\nunreachable) or \"error\".\n\nArgs:\n    host: Hostname or IP address.\n    port: TCP port number, e.g. 80, 443, 8080.\n", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"host": {"title": "Host", "type": "string"}, "port": {"title": "Port", "type": "integer"}}, "required": ["host", "port"], "title": "check_portArguments", "type": "object"}, "outputSchema": {"properties": {"result": {"title": "Result", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["result"], "title": "check_portOutput", "type": "object"}}, {"name": "check_http", "description": "Send an HTTP GET request to a URL (application layer).\n\nReturns the HTTP status code and the total response time in milliseconds.\nA slow response with DNS and port working points to an application problem.\n\nArgs:\n    url: Full URL, e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:8080/\" or \"https://www.ufrgs.br/\".\n", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"url": {"title": "Url", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["url"], "title": "check_httpArguments", "type": "object"}, "outputSchema": {"properties": {"result": {"title": "Result", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["result"], "title": "check_httpOutput", "type": "object"}}, {"name": "traceroute", "description": "Trace the route (up to 10 hops) to a host.\n\nSlow (can take up to a minute). Use it only when ping fails for a remote\nhost, to find where along the path packets are lost.\n\nArgs:\n    host: Hostname or IP address.\n", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"host": {"title": "Host", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["host"], "title": "tracerouteArguments", "type": "object"}, "outputSchema": {"properties": {"result": {"title": "Result", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["result"], "title": "tracerouteOutput", "type": "object"}}, {"name": "restart_service", "description": "Restart a lab service. Only the lab services \"web\" and \"db\" are allowed.\n\nUse it only when a lab service is down (port closed). It also resets the\nweb service to normal (non-slow) mode.\n\nArgs:\n    name: Lab service name: \"web\" or \"db\".\n", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"name": {"title": "Name", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["name"], "title": "restart_serviceArguments", "type": "object"}, "outputSchema": {"properties": {"result": {"title": "Result", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["result"], "title": "restart_serviceOutput", "type": "object"}}]}}}
